      "widgets_values": [
        "Create ONE interaction reference drawing, not a chapter page, on plain cream ground/background. IMAGE 1 is Shir and Skitters together at the correct RELATIVE PHYSICAL SIZE; preserve these proportions exactly. Correct its small baseline offset: in your output ALL feet must share the ground plane, with the dragon BESIDE the foot, not closer to camera. IMAGE 2 is hatchling identity/anatomy detail only, NOT a cue to enlarge him. Full body Shir visible scalp bun to sandals, relaxed standing, looking down at dragon warmly, front three-quarter view with both feet on ground. Same depth for both characters, no perspective size tricks. Preserve normal 9-year-old head/body proportions, blue eyes, honey dark-blonde scalp-apex topknot, lilac tee, dusty-rose shorts, pink sport sandals with black sole/straps, pink backpack with rear print occluded. Skitters light turquoise, amber eyes, yellow belly, apricot wing membranes, ivory rounded horn buds, forehead golden star. Four legs, two separate wings, one tail. Shoulder 18cm compared with Shir 130cm; snout-to-rump length 30cm excluding tail, head top roughly36cm when standing. Do not make dragon shoe-sized or knee-high at shoulder. Preserve drawing style. No egg, dimensions, lettering, labels, scenery, inset or duplicate character. Entire tail and all support contacts visible. Plenty of plain margin below soles. Skitters stands BESIDE Shir right sandal, facing towards her foot from the outside. Both tiny FRONT paws rest gently on the toe strap of her sandal; both HIND paws remain planted on the ground, his whole torso extends OUTSIDE the shoe, belly above ground and tail extends away. Front paws are raised only the small height of the sandal. Do not stack his body onto her foot or stand him upright. Slight side-on view of dragon allows clear contact and his full length.",
